   "title": "Choosing an antibiotic: which SYNDROME → which BUGS → the NARROWEST empiric drug → narrow again when cultures return",
   "lines": [
    "only for BACTERIA: not fever alone, not viruses",
    "WHEN: sepsis IMMEDIATELY · stable subacute (osteomyelitis) can wait · mild infection in a healthy patient: none",
    "the patient changes it: site, age, kidneys, allergies, immune status, pregnancy (β-lactams SAFEST) · check interactions",
    "PENICILLIN allergy reported? assess it first (ALLERGY chart): going broad ↑ C. difficile, methicillin-resistant S. aureus (MRSA)"
   ]
  },
